# CaseRelay portal — environment template.
#
#   cp .env.local.example .env.local
#
# Next.js loads .env.local automatically, so no sourcing step here (unlike the
# backend, which has no dotenv loader at all — see the repo-root .env.example).
#
# Nothing in this file is a credential. CONTROL_PLANE_SA is a service account
# *email*, not a key: the BFF signs in as you via `gcloud auth application-default
# login` and then asks IAM to mint an ID token as that account. Possessing the
# email grants nothing without roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator on it.
#
# Only CONTROL_PLANE_URL, CONTROL_PLANE_SA and NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOT_ENABLED are read
# in local development. Everything below the WIF heading is for a Vercel deploy.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — pick ONE of the two control-plane targets
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Option A — the deployed control plane (default; nothing else to run).
# Requires: ADC, roles/iam.serviceAccountTokenCreator on the SA below, and that SA
# already holds roles/run.invoker on the service (it does).
CONTROL_PLANE_URL=https://caserelay-control-plane-6nwo7o4bbq-uc.a.run.app

# Service account the BFF impersonates to mint the ID token. Required for Option A:
# user ADC cannot mint an ID token with a custom audience, only a service account can.
# Ignored entirely under Option B.
CONTROL_PLANE_SA=caserelay-portal@caserelay.iam.gserviceaccount.com

# Option B — a control plane you are running yourself on port 8000. An http:// URL
# makes controlPlaneAuthHeaders() skip auth altogether, so this path needs no Google
# credentials in the portal at all. Comment out both lines above if you use it.
# CONTROL_PLANE_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED — chat panel
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Shows the CopilotKit chat surface. The agent URL is derived from
# CONTROL_PLANE_URL server-side, so no credential reaches the browser. Any value
# other than the exact string "true" renders the disabled indicator instead.
NEXT_PUBLIC_COPILOT_ENABLED=true

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY-ONLY — the password gate on the hosted portal
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The sign-in screen in the app takes any password: it chooses which persona to
# show, and is not a check. What actually keeps the hosted portal private is the
# HTTP Basic gate in src/middleware.ts, which sits in front of the API proxy as
# well as the pages.
#
# Leave both unset locally — with no password configured the gate stands aside
# in development, and refuses to serve anything at all in a production build,
# so a secret that fails to mount cannot quietly publish the case list.
#
# infra/deploy_portal.sh sets these on Cloud Run: the username as an ordinary
# environment variable, the password mounted from the Secret Manager secret
# `caserelay-portal-password`. Read or rotate it with:
#   gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=caserelay-portal-password --project=caserelay
#   CASERELAY_PORTAL_PASSWORD=... bash infra/deploy_portal.sh
# PORTAL_AUTH_USER=admin@caserelay.com
# PORTAL_AUTH_PASSWORD=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEPLOY-ONLY — Workload Identity Federation, for a Vercel deployment
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set these instead of CONTROL_PLANE_SA when running on Vercel: its OIDC token is
# exchanged for short-lived GCP credentials, so no long-lived secret is stored.
# GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL_ID being set takes precedence over CONTROL_PLANE_SA,
# and all four must be present together or token minting throws.
# The portal is hosted on Cloud Run, not Vercel, and there it runs as the service
# account directly — so these stay unset unless someone deploys it to Vercel too.
# GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER=189353698936
# GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL_ID=vercel
# GCP_WORKLOAD_IDENTITY_POOL_PROVIDER_ID=vercel
# GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_EMAIL=caserelay-portal@caserelay.iam.gserviceaccount.com
